  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266225/assets/cebd0527c2b8b3bcdf2948da0771103f17412ff058d74b96db1287a7046ba3bc.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n* The period of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
